{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me","id":23608,"title":"Exigents for you (and me)!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-05T01:16:09-08:00","id":23608,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon10.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Exigents for you (and me)!","content":"Exalted 3rd edition is just around the corner (fingers crossed), but even being generous we're not likely to see Exalted: The Exigents until the 4th quarter of 2014, and possibly not until 2015. That is kind of a bummer since, of the new material that we're getting in 3rd edition, Exigents are by far the thing I am most excited about.<br /> <br /> Still, I figure, why wait? Once the 3rd edition corebook is out, and we have the full ruleset for Exalted 3rd edition, I imagine it won't be impossible to start creating charms and designing Exigent Exalted.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, creating an entire Exalted splat is difficult; designing and balancing charms isn't exactly easy. And with Exigents, you're looking at dozens, if not hundreds of different &quot;splats&quot; each with their own charms. Writing up a dozen Exigents, even if you just have a very basic charmset for each, to include in a chronicle is going to be a pretty major undertaking, one that I don't imagine most people want to bother with.<br /> <br /> That's where this thread comes in. I imagine that fan-made Exigents will be fairly popular in many Exalted games, even just as NPCs, simply because it will be a useful way to include Exigents without having to spend the time to write up charms or concept yourself.<br /> <br /> So this thread is designed for people to post their Exigent plans, so that other forum goers will know what to look forward to.<br /> <br /> What sort of Exigent do you plan to create? What sort of charms are you looking at? How many charms do you imagine writing? Even if you're just thinking of writing a half-dozen or so charms to give an idea of what the Exigent does, that's perfectly cool.<br /> <br /> I am currently working on an Exigent of Arilak, the goddess of the Eastern jungles and dinosaurs(!). Obviously without the mechanics here's not a lot I can do, but I have a fair number of charms laid out and prepped. I'm drawing inspiration from things like the Mokole, Jurassic Park and even that old fighting game, Primal Rage. Hopefully within a couple of months after the 3rd edition corebook gets released I'll have a functional Exigent with charmset to post on the forums.<br /> <br /> How about other people?<br /> <br /> AnubisXy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T04:22:52-08:00","id":23672,"title":"","content":"Anu, <br /> Have you considered Tarzan or even Turok? Mixing Magitech with primitive weapons would really suit the concept your going for. <br /> Considering it's not released yet I'm unaware if Extingents even have an Anima banner but I imagine a Tyrant Lizard with jungle drums in the air as his/her aura. <br /> As for my concepts... I was wondering if I could even convert Nocturnals across. Sounds like a sweet idea. My other one would be an Exalted of Lytek. <br /> What say you brother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T04:24:13-08:00","id":23674,"title":"","content":"The one I've done the most work for is the chosen of Alidrisi (original god. Domain: maps and cartographers) and I've discovered that writing Charm trees is HARD. I wanted to draw off the Infernal trees, how the curve around and interconnect, but that turned into too much work for too little reward, so I broke it down into a set of your basic branching trees and went from there. Some ideas I like:<br /> <br /> Gnat Dance: Depending on how the Onslaught mechanic works, this could go a couple different ways. 1) bleed off your Onslaught to pump up your Dodge temporarily. 2) Dodge while maintaining Onslaught.<br /> <br /> Frog Deceives Scorpion: Counter-unexpected. Burn some motes and willpower on an Unexpected attack to attempt to dodge. If you succeed, you get a counterattack.<br /> <br /> Perfected Pictograph Form: Allows drawing maps with a legend that's (magically) self-explanatory. Anyone can read this map, regardless of literacy or lack thereof. Leads to Elusive Context Interpolation.<br /> <br /> Elusive Context Interpolation: Makes a map legible by some target (specified on activation) and no one else. It's essentially Wind-Carried Words Technique in written form.<br /> <br /> Inscribing Anima: I got this idea from the label maker at work. The Exalt uses his anima to heat paper and singe it in specific patters, letting him put words and line drawings on it in a matter of moments.<br /> <br /> One Found, One Kept: I wanted this as a variation on Dread Panapoly of the Silent Wind and pals- that whole school of charms that lets you make stuff disappear and draw it back when you need it. This one can only banish things of a set Resources value (decided when you activate it the first time) for dirt-cheap. The trick, is, though, that you always need to leave something banished- pulling out the last item in your stockpile costs a ton of motes and some ahl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T04:39:54-08:00","id":23675,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if the system is still going to be one of burn motes plus Willpower for effect anymore. I seem to recall Morke saying something along those lines... or was it Holden? <br /> Give me a bit. I'll find it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T05:09:41-08:00","id":23685,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to cobble together a few bare bones frames to drape once 3E comes out. Most are probably going to be Quick NPCs with some utility charms and maybe a neat trick or two.<br /> <br /> Talk about how the various Exigents can/can't pass on their Exaltation prompted me to start thinking of different lineage avenues. I'm trying to work up something for what I'm tentatively calling The Son of Dunes*, an Exigent of a long gone lieutenant of Ahlat. The Son would basically have a term limit of [x] years, after which a tournament is held. Winner of the tournament gets the Exigency passed on to them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Like Princes of the Earth, the Son can be anywhere on the gender spectrum.</span><br /> <br /> For Charm structure, I'm going to steal the idea from (either one of the freelancers or a comment made on the old forums) and have a limited number of permanent charms, with the ability to spend XP to upgrade those permanent capabilities. Probably make it relatively simple and say that becoming The Son gets you a permanent Charm for each Attribute, which you then spend your time refining/upgrading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T06:31:49-08:00","id":23714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>edgewalker22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=23674#post23674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one I've done the most work for is the chosen of Alidrisi (original god. Domain: maps and cartographers)</div> </div> </div> </div> Forgive me for saying this, but I'm a little disappointed there's no charm called Here There Be Monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T07:30:58-08:00","id":23747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=23672#post23672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anu,<br /> As for my concepts... I was wondering if I could even convert Nocturnals across. Sounds like a sweet idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm heading that project once 3e rolls out.<br /> <br /> I'm also making the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/302-upon-the-rock-of-tradition-memorials-upcoming-fan-splat\">Memorials</a> with Kyeudo right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T07:50:11-08:00","id":23755,"title":"","content":"There is only one possible answer to me: Reimu Hakurei, or Sanae Kochiya","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T10:51:11-08:00","id":23837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=23672#post23672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anu,<br /> Have you considered Tarzan or even Turok? Mixing Magitech with primitive weapons would really suit the concept your going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>There will be a little Tarzan in there too. You can't draw power from the goddess of jungles without the classics. I hadn't though too much about primitive weaponry; I had been planning on having &quot;living&quot; weaponry, like Dragon King vegitative technology being part of her charmset. But, primitive weaponry sounds pretty snazzy. Maybe have a cascade for fighting with normal, easily broken weapons (such as bone or wood) or even having charms for using improvised weapons. I think I'll work that in. Thanks for the idea!<br /> <br /> As for Nocternals, as mentioned there's a project from several forum-goers to convert them. I'm sure they wouldn't mind some help if you'd like to jump in. An Exalted of Lytek could be cool. I've considered it a few times, but I'm not really sure what the Exalted of the god of Exaltations would do. That theme is little too esoteric for me to wrap my mind around. What sort of ideas are you looking at?<br /> <br /> AnubisXy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T11:04:56-08:00","id":23842,"title":"","content":"I want to create an Exigent that is like a sleek, high-tech android. This would differ from an Alchemical because they would not be made of clay or flesh, but of metal, glass, and other exotic materials pulled from the Wyld. All physical Charms would be internal (like Inspector Gadget). This Exigent's aesthetics would be sleek, high-tech, something that would remind you of something out of TRON: Legacy, I Am Robot or even EDI (from Mass Effect 3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T11:42:38-08:00","id":23863,"title":"","content":"Wulf: Is there a god of artifical life/mechanical sapience/inorganic life? They'd make a good choice for the Exalter of that particular Exigent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=23675#post23675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if the system is still going to be one of burn motes plus Willpower for effect anymore. I seem to recall Morke saying something along those lines... or was it Holden?<br /> Give me a bit. I'll find it</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the pertinent combat resource is, it uses a generous amount of it, so it has to be used judiciously, is the point. &quot;Dodge+counterattack&quot; is a nasty one-two, so it needs to be harder than &quot;you take me by surprise? No, I take YOU by surprise.&quot; Ideally, this would be a charm that would not be activated even in many situations where it could be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=23714#post23714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Forgive me for saying this, but I'm a little disappointed there's no charm called Here There Be Monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I am a complete idiot for not hitting on that. It is now being written. The pattern spiders will retroactively add it as soon as it's finished. (Too bad &quot;Ultima Thule&quot; is out of flavor.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T23:37:00-08:00","id":24211,"title":"","content":"Dragragonmystic: You are a golden god ... Anu: Well I'd considered that an exalted of the god of exaltation would be a chronicler of some sort. Maybe following around a circle to see what great events they would accomplish... I also figured Lytek was likely the type to use one as a personal aid. Just pulling at strings here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T23:51:17-08:00","id":24214,"title":"","content":"I've never even thought of designing my own charm tree before. However, first thing I'm building Exigent-wise is going to be a Chosen of Plentimon. The charm tree would probably involve using cards and dice as throwing weapons, using subtle bendings of fate to affect one's luck, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T00:34:46-08:00","id":24224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=24214#post24214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never even thought of designing my own charm tree before. However, first thing I'm building Exigent-wise is going to be a Chosen of Plentimon. The charm tree would probably involve using cards and dice as throwing weapons, using subtle bendings of fate to affect one's luck, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mat Cauthon from the Wheel of Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T01:55:50-08:00","id":24242,"title":"","content":"There was a fire god mentioned in Masters of Jade who's working with the Guild... it seems like someone who might have the pull to pull of an Exigent for itself. Not to mention pyromancy+tons of money seems like a fun combination!<br /> <br /> &quot;You burned down our town hall!<br /> /gives sack of money)<br /> &quot;Build a new one.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T08:47:52-08:00","id":24374,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about the Chosen of Artificial Flight in a Heaven's Reach setting. The biggest hurdle seems to be transposing Vanileth into a setting where, instead of having lost almost all of his power and prestige, he dominates everything. Would he still dislike spells because most of his purview comes from technology, or would the genre conventions place sorcery well within his purview? Or would the Chosen of Artificial Flight have Occult on their Caste Abilities anyway because it's part of how Vanileth crafts his enchanted flying machines?<br /> <br /> Charm design is also tricky. The Ability model is easier to work with and I have some interesting ideas for Bureaucracy charms based on artificial flight, but I'm drawing blank on abilities like Linguistics. The Alchemical model reflects a technology-based Exalt very well, but I'm not interested in cybernetics and it's really important to the way Alchemicals work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T08:55:55-08:00","id":24379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>edgewalker22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=23863#post23863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wulf: Is there a god of artifical life/mechanical sapience/inorganic life? They'd make a good choice for the Exalter of that particular Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is now. Thank you for this idea. I was actually stuck, for some reason, on what kind of god would create such an Exigent. It makes perfect sense for such a god to exist, too, given Animating Intelligences and such. Oh, I'm three shades of excited to start fleshing this idea out. Cheers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T09:39:51-08:00","id":24398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list\"> Fuel for Exigents: the homebrew God List - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Let's make a list of all the custom gods from people's campaigns, and prep them for Exigence. -Name: Han Dei Fang -Purview: Knowledge and texts burned -Description: A bald man of middle-height, skin composed of pages in various stages of burning. Clothes of ash. Red-hot cinders for eyes and teeth. -Reasons </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This one's a little old, but I hope it helps.<br /> That, and if anyone can help me stat up an Exigent of Han Dei Fang or Mariska, I would be delighted. Or maybe I'll do it myself and make it a PEACH thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T12:38:06-08:00","id":25297,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking Chosen of the God of Equipment/Artifacts. One Innate Power and One Charm tree:<br /> <br /> Charm Tree: An expanded and generalized version of the Solar Call the Blade Melee tree which lets you store a very large amount of equipment/artifacts elsewhere and summon them forth again. Also a charm which let you instantly don armor, if they still have a time requirement on that.<br /> <br /> Innate Power: the ability to learn Evocations like a Solar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l10FwJpUibI\" target=\"_blank\">Yes, I have been watching Fairy Tail recently, why do you ask?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T12:48:30-08:00","id":25972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me?p=24398#post24398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ebrew-god-list</a><br /> <br /> This one's a little old, but I hope it helps.<br /> That, and if anyone can help me stat up an Exigent of Han Dei Fang or Mariska, I would be delighted. Or maybe I'll do it myself and make it a PEACH thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I'm not very crunchy, but I'd imagine the Chosen of Han Dei Fang's powers would work a lot like Enrico Pucci's or Rohan Kishibe's Stands, allowing her to steal and use information from people and objects. Also, as Han Dei Fang's Chosen, she'd have access to a ton of esoterica from his library (I was THIS close to naming a charm &quot;Occluse Hipster Strike.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Anima power: The ability to &quot;devour&quot; texts, destroying the words as she reads them. This would manifest as ink streaming off the page and flowing into her eyes, or other appropriate representations. She can subsequently recall, with perfect accuracy, any text devoured this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/739-edgewalker22","name":"edgewalker22","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar739_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T11:10:23-08:00","id":26611,"title":"","content":"Well, first off. For a story idea I have:<br /> <br /> The 5 Chosen of Swan Dragon, from the Contagion. Made to be his lieutenants as he rallied the South. Destined to be forgotten and lost. One, maybe two left. Searching for their lost Imbuer. (I don't care if Exigents were even possible back then. They are in my Exalted now!) Still not sure what they'd be like in Charmset though, especially in a way to not be like 'Solar-Lite'<br /> <br /> <br /> The Chosen of Storms. Not sure which. But rather elemental in nature, Wind, Lightning, etc. Charms probably some sort of combination of Wind auras and 'controlly' attacks, lightning based attacks, that sort of thing. It's a very 'visual' concept to me. Likely will be drawing from Wind and Water Aspect DBs at least a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T11:35:27-08:00","id":26624,"title":"","content":"I'm already planning the &quot;Royal Guard&quot; of Verumipra, which will be a group of Exigent given to the Warden of Exiles after proving himself to be able to stand against the host of hell. Their exaltation is not a &quot;one shot&quot;- instead it is a ceremony in which the Verumipra mark his Chosen and &quot;exile him&quot;. In order for the ritual to work the person must be detached from all of society, without any positive physical or spiritual attachments, and when the ceremony is over, the newly exalted Exigent is also exiled from Fate. I'm still not sure about how many of them are there (between 5 to 20) and what their castes/ aspects would be, or if there is a limited number of them or that they could create more of them from any person which answers the requirements without limit. What I do have in mind is that the ceremony was designed in a way that it gets its power from any god which would hold the mantle of &quot;Warden of Exiles&quot;, so if Verumipra would eventually be killed or tempted by demons the ceremony would still work without creating exalted which are attributed to him, but to the new Warden.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I plan them to be some kind of &quot;Infernals of Heaven&quot;. They have powers over demons and can force them to obey them through a system named as &quot;Geotia&quot;. They can also bind a number of first circle demons in a way they could be easily summoned, by forcing them into an illusory form and name (I was thinking for 72 as the limit, because Geotia :P). They also have powers which are based upon them being &quot;exiled&quot;- like lowering their presence, erasing information about someone or making someone into a social outcast. I think about making them ability based. That's it for now :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}